# Complete Collision Dashboard — backend .env.example (repo root)
# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in real values, OR export these
# directly in your shell. Never commit a real .env.
#
# IMPORTANT — a real bug happened on this exact project from a stale
# exported shell variable silently overriding a .env file (python-dotenv
# does NOT override an already-exported env var). Before starting the
# API server, always run:
#   env | grep -i DATABASE
# and unset DATABASE_URL / DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED if anything unexpected
# is already exported in your shell, to be sure you're pointed at the
# branch you think you are.

# Which env var name the API reads its connection string from (see
# app/api.py's get_db_env_var()). Defaults to DATABASE_URL if unset.
COLLISION_DB_ENV_VAR=DATABASE_URL

# Neon Postgres connection string for the branch/role you intend to hit.
# - staging branch, collision_app role: safe day-to-day dev target, but
#   collision_app has NO INSERT grant on platform.person (see app/db.py's
#   module docstring) — some flows (creating brand-new people) will fail
#   under this role by design.
# - staging branch, neondb_owner role: full write access, used for this
#   cycle's end-to-end smoke testing (job create/transition/cost-entry).
# NEVER point this at the production branch from a dev machine.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://collision_app@ep-bold-leaf-a5dr4amg.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require&channel_binding=require

# Run the API locally (never auto-started by anything in this repo):
#   uvicorn app.api:app --reload --port 8002
# Port 8002, not 8000 — this Neon project is shared across several
# parallel-built dashboards (VLS/Elektrica/Complete Collision/Shell) that
# may run their own local backends concurrently on the same machine;
# 8000 collided with a sibling backend during this build.
